## Check When Done

- A compound paused for two weeks shows nothing due for fourteen days, and none
  of those days reads as missed.
- Backdating a pause reclassifies past missed days to blank with no migration
  and no backfill.
- A twelve-week cycle paused ten days finishes ten days later, with
  `cycle_end_date` unchanged in the database.
- Pausing a stack pre-ticks all members; unticking one leaves it running;
  resuming the stack does not resume a member that was paused separately.
- A compound with an indefinite pause cannot receive a second one.
- Resuming a pause today makes today due, not tomorrow.
- A pause with an end date resumes with no job having run — confirm by pausing
  until yesterday and reopening the app with no network.
- A compound paused indefinitely shows no runway estimate rather than a huge one.
- Pausing a compound does not archive it — it still appears in Stock and in its
  stack.
- Reordering `dose_times` does not relabel the times on past logged doses.
- Dropping a compound from 3× to 2× daily leaves its historic third doses visible.
- Migration numbers are unique and applied in order, with the `ALTER TYPE` in
  `014` run as its own statement.
- Pausing an already-paused compound edits the existing pause instead of stacking
  a second one.
- An every-third-day compound paused a week resumes on its original grid.
- A run ending on a fixed date, paused ten days mid-way, ends ten days later —
  and `cycle_end_date` in the database is unchanged.
- A paused compound sends no dose reminders and no low-stock nudge.
- The Next line on the detail sheet skips dates inside the pause.
- A soft-deleted compound does not appear in the paused count.
- A fully paused stack shows as one entry, not as its members.
- A part-used 1 kg tub added at ½ starts at 500 g; a part-used 100-tab bottle at
  ½ starts at 50 tabs.
- Undoing the evening dose of a twice-daily compound offline leaves the morning
  dose logged after the next hydration.
- A one-off log deleted offline stays deleted after hydration, and a replayed
  one-off log does not double-insert.
- Pause survives an offline round trip and a reinstall; un-pausing offline is not
  undone by the next hydration.
- `isDueOnFor` is still pure and synchronous, with no awaits added.
- A 1 kg creatine tub logged 10 g shows 990 g. Logged 200 times, it shows 0, not
  a negative, and the log still writes.
- A peptide vial rejects a dose in grams; a powder tub rejects a dose in IU.
- Adding creatine from scratch offers a stock step and never mentions BAC water.
- Adding stock opens on the compound's own form every time — a peptide on powder
  and BAC water, an anabolic on mg/mL, a vitamin on tabs and strength, a tub on
  weight. The form picker never opens on reconstituted by default, and does not
  appear at all when a compound has one possible form.
- A 100-tab bottle of 1000 mg vitamin C logged 2000 mg drops to 98 tabs.
- A 5000 IU vitamin D tablet can be stocked, and logging 5000 IU drops it one
  tablet.
- A multivitamin with no stated strength can be stocked as 60 tabs and logged as
  1 tab.
- No column named for milligrams holds a value in IU.
- No inventory type's stock form displays a subtext hint.
- Tub and bottle fill move as stock depletes; a part-used tub added at ½ starts
  at half.
- A 2× daily compound logs twice in one day, producing two rows, and reads 1 of
  2 after one.
- Existing single-dose logs are unchanged after the slot migration.
- A one-off log appears in the timeline and nowhere else — not in consistency,
  the runway, Stock, or the picker.
- Two one-off logs of the same thing on the same day both persist.
- The detail sheet has no `More` and no `Close`, and its fill matches the fill on
  the storage card.
- Every new table has an explicit `GRANT … TO authenticated`.
- The app still runs against a database missing every migration in this spec.